def get_slide_data() -> dict:
    return {
        'title': 'Sampling Methodology & CCD Design Space',
        'content': '\n## Design of Experiments (DoE)\n\nTo perform Surrogate-Based Optimization (SBO), we must first map the 4D design space defined in `search_map`.\n\n---\n\n### Central Composite Design (CCD) — Primary Method\n\nA deterministic, second-order Design of Experiments used as the **default sampling strategy** in StellarOrion. CCD is ideal for fitting Response Surface Models (RSM) because it resolves both linear and quadratic curvature using the minimum possible sample count.\n\nFor **4 active design variables** ($D$, $\\theta$, $N$, $R_n$):\n\n$$N_{CCD} = 2^d + 2d + 1 = 2^4 + 8 + 1 = \\mathbf{25 \\text{ Samples}}$$\n\n| Point Type | Count | Role |\n|:---|:---:|:---|\n| **Full Factorial Corners** 🔴 | $2^4 = 16$ | Probe all hypercube vertices — variable interactions |\n| **Axial / Star Points** 🔵 | $2 \\times 4 = 8$ | ±α along each axis — isolates per-parameter curvature |\n| **Centre Point** 🟢 | $1$ | Baseline / design midpoint — anchors RSM fit |\n\n---\n\n### How Far Do We Move? — Defining α (the Step Size)\n\nThe **axial distance** $\\alpha$ controls how far the star points extend *beyond* the factorial cube along each axis. StellarOrion uses **Face-Centred CCD** ($\\alpha = 1$), meaning star points sit exactly on the faces of the design hypercube — not outside it.\n\n**Why $\\alpha = 1$?**\n\n| α type | α value | Star point location | Pros | Cons |\n|:---|:---:|:---|:---|:---|\n| Face-Centred (FC) | **1.0** | On cube face | Stays inside bounds, no extrapolation risk | Slightly less rotatability |\n| Rotatable | $2^{d/4} \\approx 2.0$ | Outside cube | Perfect variance uniformity | Requires extrapolation outside design space |\n| Spherical | $\\sqrt{d} \\approx 2.0$ | On sphere | Uniform distance from centre | Points outside physical bounds |\n\nFor HIAD optimisation, extrapolation outside the physical bounds (e.g. $D > 4.5$ m or $\\theta > 75°$) is physically invalid and computationally expensive. $\\alpha = 1$ is therefore the **safe and correct choice**.\n\n**How each bound is set** (from `StellarOrionEngineMach5Up.py` `search_map`):\n\n$$[\\text{min}, \\text{max}] = [\\text{base} - \\Delta, \\;\\text{base} + \\Delta]$$\n\nThe star point at $\\alpha = 1$ on parameter $p$ lands exactly at $p = \\text{min}$ or $p = \\text{max}$, whilst all other parameters stay at the centre.\n\n| Parameter | Symbol | Min ($-\\alpha$) | Centre | Max ($+\\alpha$) | Δ |\n|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| HIAD Diameter | $D$ | 2.5 m | 3.0 m | 4.5 m | ±1.0 m (asymm.) |\n| Half-cone Angle | $\\theta$ | 45° | 60° | 75° | ±15° |\n| Toroid Count | $N$ | 3 | 6 | 9 | ±3 |\n| Nose Radius | $R_n$ | 0.50 m | 0.55 m | 0.60 m | ±0.05 m |\n\n---\n\n### CCD Sample Distribution Plot\n\nThe scatter matrix below shows all **25 CCD points** projected pairwise across the 4D space. The dashed boundary box is the design hypercube. Cross-hair lines mark where the axial (star) points pierce each face.\n\n<div style="text-align:center; margin: 1.2rem 0;">\n  <img src="figures/ccd_25_sample_distribution.png"\n       style="max-width:820px; width:100%; border-radius:10px;\n              border:1px solid rgba(76,201,240,0.3);\n              box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);" />\n  <p style="color:#8b949e; font-size:0.78rem; margin-top:0.5rem;">\n    Figure: CCD 25-sample scatter matrix — 4D HIAD design space. Red circles = factorial corners (16), blue triangles = axial points (α=1, 8 total), green star = centre (1). Dashed border = design space hypercube.\n  </p>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n### Latin Hypercube Sampling (LHS) — Alternative\n\nLHS is available via `--doe lhs`. It generates space-filling stratified random samples (minimum $10d = 40$ samples for 4 parameters) — better for higher-dimensional spaces but non-deterministic and less efficient for RSM fitting.\n\n---\n\n## Where This Fits into the MoP SBO Workflow\n\n```\n  CCD (25 pts, α=1)       SPARTA DSMC × 25           MoP (128-128 MLP)\n  ─────────────────  →   ──────────────────────  →   ──────────────────────\n  Fixed design matrix     High-fidelity C_D +         Ultra-fast surrogate\n  over 4D parameter       q̇_stag per sample           for GA optimisation\n  space (no guessing)\n```\n'
    }
